Third-party software

This file is DireWolf's own NOTICE under section 4(d) of the Apache License. It
is not a list of third-party packages and it does not reproduce their licences.

Source. The DireWolf project distributes source code. This repository does not
vendor third-party source: dependencies are fetched by Cargo and uv from their
public registries, pinned in Cargo.lock, fuzz/Cargo.lock and uv.lock, and
remain under their own licences.

Binaries. The binaries built from this workspace (`direwolf`, `dwkd-authority`,
`dwkd-broker`) may link third-party crates, and the set each one links differs
by target platform. `dwkd-authority` compiles in the SQLite C amalgamation,
which is in the public domain. Development, test and fuzzing dependencies are
never linked into a binary. The Python packages declare their runtime
dependencies, if any, in their pyproject.toml files, locked in uv.lock.

Obligations. Whoever distributes a binary, or any other artifact that includes
third-party code, distributes that code too, and must meet the conditions of
each included package's licence for that artifact and platform:

- MIT, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, Zlib, Unicode-3.0 and Apache-2.0 require
  their copyright and licence notices to accompany binary copies;
- where a package offers a choice of licences, the licence relied on is one on
  the allowlist in deny.toml -- never a copyleft alternative such as
  GPL-2.0-only;
- a package that ships its own Apache-2.0 NOTICE file must have that notice
  reproduced with the artifact;
- where a package's published crate omits its licence text, the text is taken
  from the upstream project and reviewed before distribution.

The project generates these notices per binary and per platform from the
locked, linked dependency closure before it distributes any binary (release
integrity, docs/ROADMAP.md M18). It has not distributed binaries so far.

A licence check is not attribution. `cargo deny check licenses` restricts
dependencies to the allowlist in deny.toml. It does not produce, verify or ship
any attribution notice.
